{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Big Beat Wobble",
 "category": "Bass",
 "text": "Sound: the fat, filtered, wobbling bass of 1990s big beat and breaks: a growling saw and square opening and closing in rhythm, with some dirt on top.\n\nHow it's built: one oscillator's saw and pulse, mixed, into the Ladder filter (low CUTOFF, RESONANCE up); a triangle LFO into the CUTOFF makes the wobble, restarted by each key (RESET on the gate) so every note wobbles the same way. Drive after the filter. One voice.\n\nPlay: long held notes and slides between keys.\n\nTweak: the LFO's RATE (the speed of the wobble: try 2, 4, 6 Hz), its WAVE (Square chops, Saw down pumps), the filter's CV (how deep), DRIVE.",
 "voices": 1,
